 are finite, yet they are not equal. Therefore, the discontinuity at $x=2$ is a jump discontinuity.\n\nNote that there is also a discontinuity at $x=-1$ and $x=4,$ but they are not jump discontinuities.\n\nHence, the correct answer is $x=-3$ and $x=2$ only." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362526 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362527 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362526 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362528 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362526 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362529 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362526 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362530 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362526 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362531 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362526 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362526 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362526 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362531 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362526 1080 #uuid "a99e8036-7fde-5d5f-8af9-1b96ac504cf9" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362527 1081 "$x=-3$ and $x=4$ only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362527 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362527 1084 #uuid "77b8e229-8c0c-5996-87dc-ad6d3af6b1fb" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362528 1081 "$x=2$ only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362528 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362528 1084 #uuid "f8ec69ad-435c-547f-b809-c868c8505005" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362529 1081 "$x=-3$ only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362529 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362529 1084 #uuid "74fd8ecb-f4be-569a-ac3f-b551b4267be2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362530 1081 "$x=-1$ and $x=4$ only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362530 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362530 1084 #uuid "2bfaab