7$ and $|Y|=4,$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(X)|+|P(Y)| & ={2}^{|X|}+{2}^{|Y|} \\\\  & ={2}^{7}+{2}^{4} \\\\  & =128+16 \\\\  & =144.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362546 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362547 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362546 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362548 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362546 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362549 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362546 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362550 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362546 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362551 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362546 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362546 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362546 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362551 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362546 1080 #uuid "81ce216f-9e6b-5ea0-bdeb-30a74b57d606" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362547 1081 "16" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362547 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362547 1084 #uuid "aaf41173-6012-5f83-b7c8-114b07609441" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362548 1081 "128" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362548 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362548 1084 #uuid "1cc1b99f-c1bf-5401-8dc8-ea5f45a1da0e" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362549 1081 "2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362549 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362549 1084 #uuid "334b7a5c-2f0d-5e86-be2d-18b9e2a98ca8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362550 1081 "112" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362550 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362550 1084 #uuid "7067111c-1b1e-5b4a-8e91-2c7f60436baa" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362551 1081 "144" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362551 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362551 1084 #uuid "507acb3c-9fba-5397-9890-a9b0be0f9f83" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362552 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362553 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362552 1069 "q-105143" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362552 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362552 1071 "Suppose that $X$ and $Y$ are sets. If $|X|=1$ and $|Y|=7,$ then $|P(X)|\\cdot |P(Y)|=$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362552 1072 #uuid "22ef9164-0409-5651-b0df-ad2369bb46cf" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362552 1074 "For any set $S$, $|P(S)|={2}^{|S|}.$ \n\nIn this case, $|X|=1$ and $|Y|=7,$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(X)|\\cdot |P(Y)| & ={2}^{|X|}\\cdot {2}^{|Y|} \\\\  & ={2}^{1}\\cdot {2}^{7} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 128 \\\\  & =256.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362553 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362554 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362553 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362555 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362553 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362556 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362553 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362557 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362553 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362558 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362553 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362553 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362553 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362557 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362553 1080 #uuid "b4e90378-9aa9-5568-b0cc-8ce23e58f41c" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362554 1081 "128" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362554 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362554 1084 #uuid "3231dc3d-784f-5c44-b8dc-14ca4ce2e6be" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362555 1081 "2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362555 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362555 1084 #uuid "a70b196d-3b0a-5d37-b60f-69a008cf366b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362556 1081 "1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362556 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362556 1084 #uuid "8f30bc1f-6d3c-5e68-9945-db69ab2f9e39" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362557 1081 "256" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362557 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362557 1084 #uuid "11d501bc-373e-5b9a-b385-4c37ff0e26b0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362558 1081 "124" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362558 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362558 1084 #uuid "b9cfcec8-d7cf-5fab-a6d6-aa65f7d7c9ea" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362559 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362560 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362559 1069 "q-105443" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362559 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362559 1071 "Which of the following sets are neither open nor closed?\n\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }3x+y<8,\\,0<x<3}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }0\\le x<6,\\,2<y\\le 4}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}<6}$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362559 1072 #uuid "c082af6c-4b35-55f0-b925-7876243430ba" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362559 1074 "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *open* since it doesn't contain any point of its boundary (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The second set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(0,3).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(3,2).$\n\n- The third set is *open* since it doesn't contain any point of its boundary (the corresponding inequality is strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362560 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362561 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362560 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362562 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362560 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362563 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362560 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362564 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362560 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362565 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362560 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362560 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362560 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362565 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362560 1080 #uuid "1a3582bb-94c4-57db-bf7b-5789d14fe916" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362561 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362561 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362561 1084 #uuid "52fbd0d4-0de5-5f72-9254-f4e6e749d8bc" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362562 1081 "I only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362562 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362562 1084 #uuid "cd232d85-718b-55dd-b3bd-4959c54b256d" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362563 1081 "III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362563 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362563 1084 #uuid "8a9c45da-2cca-5062-859c-ef15e5286a9a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362564 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362564 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362564 1084 #uuid "d0fc7e25-ff19-52ea-a6b5-23084f8b905e" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362565 1081 "II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362565 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362565 1084 #uuid "f1040cc9-4da3-5149-8fd2-2917139a6e43" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362566 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362567 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362566 1069 "q-105444" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362566 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362566 1071 "Which of the following sets are neither open nor closed?\n\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,6\\le x<9,\\,0<y<2}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}<3}$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362566 1072 #uuid "8f4b0cdf-9fe1-57d6-a009-4edf0331d401" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362566 1074 "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(6,1).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(8,0).$\n\n- The second set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (the corresponding inequality is strict).\n\n- The third set is also *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (the corresponding inequality is strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139533445 17