 is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362636 1072 #uuid "29e169b1-20c5-5789-9178-14e4b85ea9c1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362636 1074 "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if ${A}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ and ${A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],$ then\n${A}_{1}$ and ${A}_{2}$ each contain a row consisting only of zeros, so they are not invertible. However,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis invertible. So, $S$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, if $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix that is not invertible then $det(A)=0$ and therefore for all $\\alpha \\in R$ \n\n$$\ndet(\\alpha A)={\\alpha }^{2}\\cdot det(A)={\\alpha }^{2}\\cdot 0=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore,  $S$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $S$ is a *not* subspace because it's not closed under addition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and IV only.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362637 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362638 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362637 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362639 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362637 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362640 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362637 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362641 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362637 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362642 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362637 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362637 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362637 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362639 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362637 1080 #uuid "45dc1888-563d-57e2-87c8-eacef8e3e71e" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362638 1081 "I and IV only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362638 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362638 1084 #uuid "e9518d52-cb17-52af-828c-ca2d05c1f181" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362639 1081 "II and IV only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362639 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362639 1084 #uuid "a2941d64-aa24-576d-bc80-dd9f6ed90e0c" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362640 1081 "I only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362640 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362640 1084 #uuid "08afe76d-888c-511f-8820-1ac6afb5ba4c" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362641 1081 "I, II, and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362641 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362641 1084 #uuid "4b936b56-fcb2-5307-a485-2bf8793efcf1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362642 1081 "IV only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362642 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362642 1084 #uuid "0fdc3f67-6458-5e56-8339-e91b6cb6f3b3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362643 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362644 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362643 1069 "q-107144" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362643 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362643 1071 "Consider the vector space $C[0,1]$ of all continuous functions $f:[0,1]\\to R$ and its subset $B={f\\in C[0,1]\\,|\\,\\,f(x)\\le 1\\,\\,∀x\\in [0,1]}.$ \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $B$ is closed under function addition\n- $B$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $B$ is a subspace of $C[0,1]$\n- $B$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362643 1072 #uuid "ff663474-9982-50d0-b983-22c1b4e4d38b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362643 1074 "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if  $f(x)=g(x)=1$ for all $x\\in [0,1]$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f+g)(x) & =f(x)+g(x) \\\\  & =1+1 \\\\  & =2 \\\\  & >1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $x\\in [0,1].$ So, $B$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. Let, for example,  $f(x)=1$ for all $x\\in [0,1]$ and take and $k=2,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(kf)(x) & =2f(x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2 \\\\  & >1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $x\\in [0,1].$ So, $B$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $B$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362644 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362645 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362644 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362646 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362644 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362647 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362644 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362648 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362644 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362649 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362644 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362644 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362644 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362648 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362644 1080 #uuid "53f9552d-e64e-5f3e-ab12-e1050c060f72" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362645 1081 "I and IV only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362645 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362645 1084 #uuid "ec283456-8469-54e5-9273-6368155316ae" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362646 1081 "II and IV only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362646 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362646 1084 #uuid "864d553e-fd54-5137-9109-7f382e7fc8ef" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362647 1081 "I, II, and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362647 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362647 1084 #uuid "6736ccec-e6d4-5ed4-9fd2-f42fe1d4525e" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362648 1081 "IV only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362648 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362648 1084 #uuid "e27cc063-b6a0-5ef8-a8eb-afe67e1565fb" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362649 1081 "II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362649 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362649 1084 #uuid "207bf73a-882c-5f28-8d6a-ac6e5dde111f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362650 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362651 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362650 1069 "q-107147" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362650 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362650 1071 "Consider the vector space $C[0,1]$ of all continuous functions $f:[0,1]\\to R$ and its subset $K$ containing all nonconstant functions.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $K$ is closed under function addition\n- $K$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $K$ is a subspace of $C[0,1]$\n- $K$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$\n\n*Hint: $f$ is a constant function if $f(x)=\\text{constant}$ for all $x\\in [0,1].$*" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362650 1072 #uuid "ecd1a414-f091-5cfd-86f0-d0c82f6d9564" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362650 1074 "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar mult