d7f55a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362703 1074 "To find the horizontal asymptote of a rational function, we divide every term in the numerator and denominator by the dominant term in the denominator, and then we let $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nIgnoring the coefficient, the dominant term in the denominator is ${x}^{5}.$ So, we divide every term in the numerator and denominator by ${x}^{5},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}+3}{8{x}^{5}+x-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{{x}^{5}}+\\frac{3}{{x}^{5}})}{(\\frac{8{x}^{5}}{{x}^{5}}+\\frac{x}{{x}^{5}}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{3}{{x}^{5}})}{(8+\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, when $x$ is very large, the terms $\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}},\\frac{3}{{x}^{5}},\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}$ and $\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}$ become very small. Therefore, as $x\\to \\infty ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{(\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{3}{{x}^{5}})}{(8+\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}})} \\\\  & \\to \\frac{0+0}{8+0-0} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the horizontal asymptote is $y=0.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362704 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362705 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362704 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362706 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362704 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362707 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362704 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362708 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362704 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362709 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362704 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362704 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362704 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362707 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362704 1080 #uuid "057b8ad9-0506-5565-9d08-c0287153ae1b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362705 1081 "y=\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362705 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362705 1084 #uuid "8b47481a-9c57-5681-9953-e1135c30b79a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362706 1081 "y=-3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362706 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362706 1084 #uuid "00af719b-641e-5240-ac2a-ee847184b8a4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362707 1081 "y=0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362707 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362707 1084 #uuid "57170c71-acd3-56b3-bee7-f6099ad727a0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362708 1081 "y=\\frac{3}{8}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362708 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362708 1084 #uuid "15755a9f-9cb1-5d94-a61d-0a5a9dae1db2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362709 1081 "y=-2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362709 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362709 1084 #uuid "e503c475-0d1d-5128-856c-b71c6e735127" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362710 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362711 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362710 1069 "q-113180" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362710 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362710 1071 "Determine the horizontal asymptote of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3x+2}.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362710 1072 #uuid "4507ae6a-461d-5502-b3e2-7bf57bad8732" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362710 1074 "To find the horizontal asymptote of a rational function, we divide every term in the numerator and denominator by the dominant term in the denominator, and then we let $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nIgnoring the coefficient, the dominant term in the denominator is $x.$ So, we divide every term in the numerator and denominator by $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3x+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{x})}{(\\frac{3x}{x}+\\frac{2}{x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(3+\\frac{2}{x})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, when $x$ is very large, the term $\\frac{2}{x}$ becomes very small. Therefore, as $x\\to \\infty ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(3+\\frac{2}{x})} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3+0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is not a constant, which means that $y=f(x)$ does not have a horizontal asymptote." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362711 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362712 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362711 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362713 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362711 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362714 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362711 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362715 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362711 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362716 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362711 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362711 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362711 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362713 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362711 1080 #uuid "219e25d5-1a5d-54bd-84e6-7016995fdf31" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362712 1081 "y=3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362712 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362712 1084 #uuid "8f3bea2c-306c-5e48-88e0-f498569d09ab" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362713 1081 "No horizontal asymptotes" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362713 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362713 1084 #uuid "10399da4-e690-5c4d-b2a4-9bff2c1171d9" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362714 1081 "y=\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362714 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362714 1084 #uuid "a1078051-