n{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362945 1072 #uuid "fbcc8a51-42ac-5cb8-a6bc-0647017d9ba5" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362945 1074 "Notice that $Y$ can be obtained from $X$ by swapping the $2$nd and the $3$rd rows. \n\nThis changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Y) & =-det(X) \\\\  & =-(14) \\\\  & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362946 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362947 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362946 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362948 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362946 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362949 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362946 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362950 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362946 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362951 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362946 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362946 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362946 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362948 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362946 1080 #uuid "addc5023-5343-5d6e-94d4-459e9803d13f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362947 1081 "9" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362947 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362947 1084 #uuid "319beb45-da82-5928-83bf-d29bc52ed19f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362948 1081 "-14" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362948 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362948 1084 #uuid "a259e746-f501-54ae-be55-fef569b47320" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362949 1081 "3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362949 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362949 1084 #uuid "21d9eeeb-c150-51f2-9c34-5dfbb8074a06" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362950 1081 "7" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362950 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362950 1084 #uuid "ca0902b3-371c-5ed1-bcca-bdf20d2b6da8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362951 1081 "14" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362951 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362951 1084 #uuid "6227f8a3-0c1e-5bad-a5c1-bba85528c3cf" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362952 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362953 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362952 1069 "q-135457" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362952 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362952 1071 "A certain company produces two types of footwear: casual and sports. The following table describes how the number of customers changes between both types of footwear each year:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Casual** | **Sports** |\n| To: | **Casual** | $0.55$ | $0.7$ |\n| **Sports** | $0.45$ | $0.3$ |  |\n\nThat is, $45%$ of casual customers switch to sports each year, and $70%$ of sports customers change to casual.\n\nCurrently, $700\\,000$ customers purchase casual footwear, while $300\\,000$ customers purchase sports footwear. How many customers will purchase sports footwear in one year? You may assume that the total number of customers doesn't change." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362952 1072 #uuid "960aa206-ef2f-590f-b6e6-46bfb1026352" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362952 1074 "From the table, we can build the corresponding stochastic matrix: \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.55 & 0.7 \\\\ 0.45 & 0.3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe vector describing the number of customers for each type of footwear is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}700\\,000 \\\\ 300\\,000\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nDividing the vector above by the total number of customers $(1\\,000\\,000),$ we get the stochastic vector of the initial state:\n\n$$\n{x}_{0}=\\frac{1}{1\\,000\\,000}[\\begin{aligned}700\\,000 \\\\ 300\\,000\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0.7 \\\\ 0.3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the state vector ${x}_{1}$ after one year, we apply one step of the Markov chain:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=P{x}_{0}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =P{x}_{0} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.55 & 0.7 \\\\ 0.45 & 0.3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0.7 \\\\ 0.3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.595 \\\\ 0.405\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after one year, $40.5%$ of customers will purchase sports footwear. Computing $40.5%$ of $1\\,000\\,000,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n1\\,000\\,000\\cdot 0.405=405\\,000.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $405\\,000$ customers will purchase sports footwear in one year." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362953 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362954 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362953 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362955 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362953 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362956 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362953 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362957 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362953 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362958 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362953 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362953 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362953 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362954 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362953 1080 #uuid "c01d1ab0-b4e0-570d-9f6a-3444da987d66" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362954 1081 "405\\,000" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362954 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362954 1084 #uuid "1df1090c-b953-55e7-82db-2918444fb6f3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362955 1081 "425\\,000" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362955 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362955 1084 #uuid "ddc961d6-6767-5034-8c94-13fc400c4870" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362956 1081 "395\\,000" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362956 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362956 1084 #uuid "cbec1301-90b2-5468-bdbd-75e91b591098" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362957 1081 "555\\,000" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362957 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362957 1084 #uuid "d3c54158-eb40-57d4-902a-43c93f2cbfcb" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362958 1081 "360\\,000" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362958 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362958 1084 #uuid "07a27bf2-8db9-58f0-b441-14ea9ca218eb" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362959 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362960 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362959 1069 "q-135487" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362959 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362959 1071 "Which of the following are stochastic matrices?\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}-0.1 & 0.2 \\\\ 1.1 & 0.8\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}0.1 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.9 & 0.8\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}0.5 & 0 & 0.5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0.5 & 0 & 0.5\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362959 1072 #uuid "90365b47-9514-5b9b-bb0b-216780f54607" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362959 1074 "Recall that a stochastic vector is a vector with nonnegative entries that add up to $1.$ A matrix is stochastic if all its columns are stochastic vectors.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices in turn.\n\n- Matrix $U$ is *not* a stochastic matrix since its first column is not a stochastic vector (it contains negative entries): \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-0.1 & 0.2 \\\\ 1.1 & 0.8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Matrix $V$ is a stochastic matrix. Indeed, each column is a stochastic vector (the corresponding entries are nonnegative and add up to one): \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}0.1 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.9 & 0.8\\end{aligned}]\\,\\begin{aligned}0.1+0.9=1 \\\\ 0.2+0.8=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Matrix $W$ is a stochastic matrix. Indeed, each column is a stochastic vector (the corresponding entries are non-negative and add up to one): \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}0.5 & 0 & 0.5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0.5 & 0 & 0.5\\end{aligned}]\\,\\begin{aligned}0.5+0+0.5=1 \\\\ 0+1+0=1 \\\\ 0.5+0+0.5=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$V$ and $W$ only.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362960 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362961 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362960 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362962 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362960 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362963 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362960 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362964 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362960 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362965 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362960 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362960 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362960 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362962 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362960 1080 #uuid "470f887c-a240-5a37-9fd2-2eaded721c71" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362961 1081 "$U$ and $W$ only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362961 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362961 1084 #uuid "0240ee35-bf1a-518d-b734-22e7fc2595b8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362962 1081 "$V$ and $W$ only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362962 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362962 1084 #uuid "c102312d-4f06-5ee7-bfba-19a3e85466e9" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362963 1081 "$U,$ $V,$ and $W$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362963 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362963 1084 #uuid "608e0fb6-5eed-5bfe-b2ff-5a12f96ee232" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362964 1081 "$U$ and $V$ only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362964 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362964 1084 #uuid "d00e77ed-9e7d-55d5-8191-e5d0ee50ec26" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362965 1081 "$W$ only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362965 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362965 1084 #uuid "b4fcd242-22e8-5d68-97fe-c0929b9c3ace" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362966 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362967 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362966 1069 "q-135491" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362966 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362966 1071 "In a particular town, the housekeepers use $2$ types of olive oil for preparing food: oil $A$ and oil $B.$  A study has shown that, each month \n\n- $40%$ of housekeepers who used oil $A$ swap to oil $B$, and\n\n- $30%$ of housekeepers who used oil $B$ swap to oil $A.$\n\nWhich of the following tables describes how these housekeepers change their preferences each month?" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362966 1072 #uuid "df75b222-1f6c-5b44-9ba7-24d1998fa187" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362966 1074 "We are given the following situation for each month: \n\n- $40%$ of housekeepers who used oil $A$ swap to oil $B.$ This implies that $60%$ of them remain using oil $A.$\n\n- $30%$ of housekeepers who used oil $B$ swap to oil $A.$ This implies that $70%$ of them remain using oil $B.$\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Oil $A$** | **Oil $B$** |\n| To: | **Oil $A$** | $0.6$ | $0.3$ |\n| **Oil $B$** | $0.4$ | $0.7$ |  |\n\nNote that we can write a corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0.6 & 0.3 \\\\ 0.4 & 0.7\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362967 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362968 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362967 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362969 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362967 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362970 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362967 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362971 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362967 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362972 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362967 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362967 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362967 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362969 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362967 1080 #uuid "81be96fa-a417-5d81-9fcf-9d833274bedd" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362968 1081 "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Oil $A$** | **Oil $B$** |\n| To: | **Oil $A$** | $0.4$ | $0.3$ |\n| **Oil $B$** | $0.6$ | $0.7$ |  |" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362968 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362968 1084 #uuid "c3ecc879-2c95-5f74-ac4a-ab969113e91a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362969 1081 "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Oil $A$** | **Oil $B$** |\n| To: | **Oil $A$** | $0.6$ | $0.3$ |\n| **Oil $B$** | $0.4$ | $0.7$ |  |" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362969 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362969 1084 #uuid "c3a103d0-014c-5342-a350-b00b3703cd6d" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362970 1081 "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Oil $A$** | **Oil $B$** |\n| To: | **Oil $A$** | $0.3$ | $0.6$ |\n| **Oil $B$** | $0.7$ | $0.4$ |  |" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362970 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186