\\\  & \\ge -6{x}_{1}^{2}-6{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =-6({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=1.$ So,  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2})=-6(1)=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\ge -6.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no smaller than $-6.$ But before we conclude that $-6$ is the minimum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=-6.$\n\nNotice that when $x={[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =4{x}_{1}^{2}-6{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =4(0)^{2}-6(1)^{2} \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the minimum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $-6.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363055 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363056 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363055 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363057 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363055 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363058 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363055 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363059 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363055 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363060 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363055 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363055 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363055 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363060 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363055 1080 #uuid "33e74247-61c0-5aec-9e37-8a7504fd27bd" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363056 1081 "1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363056 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363056 1084 #uuid "30b8156c-9e64-5b61-aeca-3d74ab19e687" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363057 1081 "4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363057 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363057 1084 #uuid "1202061a-84a4-5c46-9aa8-4d93661b1821" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363058 1081 "0" 1319