s examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. As we've seen, $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ contains none of its boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A=A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363139 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363140 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363139 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363141 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363139 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363142 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363139 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363143 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363139 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363144 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363139 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363139 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363139 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363140 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363139 1080 #uuid "5fce85d8-31bd-5894-a084-f12d40765a2a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363140 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363140 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363140 1084 #uuid "bd3c14e6-cdac-5b50-83d2-c7a7e936d3c5" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363141 1081 "I only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363141 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363141 1084 #uuid "7e056cb0-ca61-54f2-a5e9-73842a82ebde" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363142 1081 "III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363142 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363142 1084 #uuid "c9cb356d-0a4a-57bd-9dbf-4365785bf3de" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363143 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363143 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363143 1084 #uuid "d6fe1489-c5d9-51b7-a695-df2f0bfed8ba" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363144 1081 "II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363144 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363144 1084 #uuid "301c3c2d-1689-5485-a99c-8b0d727eadbf" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363145 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363146 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363145 1069 "q-161639" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363145 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363145 1071 "Which of the following sets are closed?\n\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<2,\\,0<y<x}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le e,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡x}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{3}}$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363145 1072 #uuid "28c149d9-63e5-5d01-abf9-5e8569624b8a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363145 1074 "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The second set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The third set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363146 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363147 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363146 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363148 13194139533445 17592186045585 true