\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}36 & -12 \\\\ -12 & 36\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we maximize ${Q}^{′}(y)$ when $‖y‖=1,$ as usual. Calculating the eigenvalues $B,$ we obtain the following:   \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|B-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}36-\\lambda  & -12 \\\\ -12 & 36-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (36-\\lambda )(36-\\lambda )-144 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-72\\lambda +1\\,152 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -48)(\\lambda -24) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =48,\\,24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nmin{{Q}^{′}(y)\\,|\\,‖y‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}=24.\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363251 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363252 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363251 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363253 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363251 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363254 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363251 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363255 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363251 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363256 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363251 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363251 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363251 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363256 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363251 1080 #uuid "9291ebf4-3b9e-5f57-b402-ac7a972ece48" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363252 1081 "28" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363252 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363252 1084 #uuid "64e88f2e-80c7-514b-b5a7-2af1c6a72c44" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363253 1081 "8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363253 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363253 1084 #uuid "0bbc315b-06ea-5fd7-95ff-4928384794a2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363254 1081 "-4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363254 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 131941