 [17592186363596 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363596 1084 #uuid "289c0370-99d1-5dbe-8e1d-e4422b14a439" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363597 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363598 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363597 1069 "q-183341" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363597 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363597 1071 "$\\,$ **If** $8$ is even **then** $4\\in {2,4,8}.$ \n\nWhich of the following statements are equivalent to the conditional statement above?\n\n- If $4\\in {2,4,8},$ then $8$ is even.\n- If $4\\notin {2,4,8},$ then $8$ is not even.\n- If $8$ is not even, then $4\\notin {2,4,8}.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363597 1072 #uuid "8d0274f7-9e96-5c91-af2a-50bf61bf0ba6" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363597 1074 "Let's recall the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.\n\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other, but not to the original statement.\n\n![](images/0d/0deb19675402bf931111bb80cb616682aac08491b5cd3e1ab5812da05b6df8a8.png)\n\nSo, we are looking for the contrapositive of the given statement.\n\n- Statement I is the converse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement II is the contrapositive. $\\,✓$\n\n- Statement III is the inverse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363598 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363599 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363598 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363600 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363598 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363601 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363598 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363602 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363598 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363603 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363598 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 175921