9 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363700 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363699 1069 "q-330299" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363699 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363699 1071 "Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfy the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t)$ and ${x}_{p}(t)$ satisfy the inhomogeneous system\n${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t)+f(t).$\nWhich of the following is **always** a solution of the same inhomogeneous system?\n\n- ${x}_{1}(t)-4\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$\n- $-7\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$\n- $2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+2\\cdot {x}_{p}(t)$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363699 1072 #uuid "ec98e74e-e68c-5045-a599-d3ec1260eaf6" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363699 1074 "Recall that if ${x}_{h}(t)$ satisfies a homogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution to an inhomogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t),$ then ${x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$ is also a solution to the same inhomogeneous system.\n\nAdditonally, the *linearity principle* for systems of linear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) states that if ${x}_{1}(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t),…,{x}_{k}(t)$ are solutions to a homogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ then any linear combination \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)+⋯+{c}_{k}{x}_{k}(t)\n$$\n\nwith ${c}_{1},{c}_{2},…,{c}_{k}\\in R$ is also a solution of the same homogeneous system. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given expression.\n\n- Option I is a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Indeed, notice that the linear combination \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)=1\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-4\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ according to the linearity principle. Thus, \n\n$$\n{{{x}_{1}(t)-4\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{h}(t)}+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to our inhomogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t).$\n\n- Option II is a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Indeed, notice that the linear combination \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)=-7\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ according to the linearity principle. Thus, \n\n$$\n{{-7\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{h}(t)}+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to our inhomogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t).$\n\n- Option III might be *not* a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Notice that $2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+2\\cdot {x}_{p}(t)$ can't be written as \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{h}(t)$ is a solution of the homogeneous system, because of the multiplier $2$ next to the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363700 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363701 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363700 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363702 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363700 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363703 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363700 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363704 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363700 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363705 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363700 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363700 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363700 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363704 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363700 1080 #uuid "160e5d13-0f83-577a-91ea-265646d1a7fc" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363701 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363701 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363701 1084 #uuid "11f20d51-8248-5571-8f98-e7ef675035c8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363702 1081 "I only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363702 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363702 1084 #uuid "cd02aaba-65be-57fc-b02b-376ab809d02c" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363703 1081 "III 