b/ref 17592186363710 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363707 1080 #uuid "3917585f-6220-5ca1-94fd-e86e8a7709e8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363708 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363708 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363708 1084 #uuid "0dce4286-552d-5198-8e60-ae77cf3ff5fc" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363709 1081 "I only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363709 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363709 1084 #uuid "95a5e686-1269-5d81-a1dd-9ff2c45dcc71" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363710 1081 "III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363710 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363710 1084 #uuid "2186a39d-4c02-5910-b7fb-1213d1919bbc" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363711 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363711 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363711 1084 #uuid "fdbd7686-2587-593e-9a8d-997b6f64f602" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363712 1081 "II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363712 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363712 1084 #uuid "ab32738a-ed25-573a-a522-733662acefce" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363713 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363714 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363713 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363716 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363713 1069 "q-333273" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363713 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363713 1071 "Consider the following initial value problem for the functions $y=y(x),z=z(x):$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}=x(y-z),\\, & y(0)=-1 \\\\ {z}^{′}=y(z-x),\\, & z(0)=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse Euler's method with two steps of equal size to approximate $y(1)$ and $z(1).$\n\n$y(1)≈$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,z(1)≈$\n{{field-2}}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363713 1072 #uuid "ba386268-3918-5f5f-b2cc-ec302545ce83" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363713 1074 "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}=f(x,y,z),\\, & y(a)=c, \\\\ {z}^{′}=g(x,y,z),\\, & z(a)=d,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEuler's method approximates the solution by applying the update rule component-wise to each equation. More precisely, the increments on $y$ and $z$ are\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}Δy={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx, \\\\ Δz={z}^{′}\\cdot Δx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe new values are then given by ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and ${z}_{\\text{new}}=z+Δz.$\n\nFirst, note that we are given the values of $y$ and $z$ at $x=0$ and asked to find their values at $x=1.$ The distance from $x=0$ to $x=1$ is $1,$ and since we are asked to use two steps of equal size, our step size must be\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{1-0}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with Euler's method. We'll start by creating a table that includes the initial condition data $y(0)=-1$ and $z(0)=-1.$\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $-1$ |  |  | $-1$ |  |  |\n\n**Step 1**.\n\nWe compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy,$ ${z}^{′}$ and $Δz$ (using the values of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ in the first row), and the values of ${x}_{\\text{new}},$ ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ and ${z}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =x(y-z)=0(-1-(-1))=0 \\\\ {z}^{′} & =y(z-x)=-1(-1-0)=1 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=0\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=0 \\\\ Δz & ={z}^{′}\\cdot Δx=1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=0+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=-1+0=-1 \\\\ {z}_{\\text{new}} & =z+Δz=-1+\\frac{1}{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add these values to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $0$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-1$ |  |  | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ |  |  |\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nWe compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy,$ ${z}^{′}$ and $Δz$ (using the values of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ in the second row), and the values of ${x}_{\\text{new}},$ ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ and ${z}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =x(y-z)=\\frac{1}{2}(-1-(-\\frac{1}{2}))=-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {z}^{′} & =y(z-x)=-1(-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2})=1 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=-\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=-\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ Δz & ={z}^{′}\\cdot Δx=1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=1 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=-1+(-\\frac{1}{8})=-\\frac{9}{8} \\\\ {z}_{\\text{new}} & =z+Δz=-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add these values to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $0$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-1$ | $-\\frac{1}{4}$ | $-\\frac{1}{8}$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $1$ | $-\\frac{9}{8}$ |  |  | $0$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n$y(1)≈-\\frac{9}{8}$\nand\n$z(1)≈0.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363714 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363715 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363714 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363714 1077 "field-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363714 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363715 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363714 1080 #uuid "5f9782ff-09d0-5e25-85d1-e4414ec19796" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363715 1081 "-\\frac{9}{8}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363715 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363715 1084 #uuid "073e29c7-0791-52b8-85a1-d99563246a47" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363716 1075 #edb/ref 17