er's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ Δz & ={z}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add these to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $-2$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-1$ | $-3$ | $-\\frac{3}{4}$ |\n\nTo get the new values of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ in the *next* row, we add $Δx$ to $x,$ $Δy$ to $y,$ and $Δz$ to $z,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=0+\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=1+(-\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {z}_{\\text{new}} & =z+Δz=-1+(-\\frac{3}{4})=-\\frac{7}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these values to our table in a new row gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $-2$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-1$ | $-3$ | $-\\frac{3}{4}$ |\n| $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |  |  | $-\\frac{7}{4}$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n$y\\,(\\frac{1}{4})≈\\frac{1}{2}$\nand\n$z\\,(\\frac{1}{4})≈-\\frac{7}{4}.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363724 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363725 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363724 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363724 1077 "field-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363724 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363725 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363724 1080 #uuid "1656d3a8-00dc-5980-b9eb-4de66cbd6595" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363725 1081 "-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363725 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363725 1084 #uuid "4308ef05-e8cd-52d8-8b61-818e73f777ee" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363726 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363727 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363726 10