186363877 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363877 1071 "$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=6x$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ The Fourier sine series of the **odd** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the expression for ${b}_{n}.$$\\,{b}_{n}=$ {{field-1}}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363877 1072 #uuid "c4e611af-caa9-51f2-a7d5-41c09f3cb745" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363877 1074 "For our Fourier sine series, the coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=6x$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{12}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\, & ⇒\\,v=-\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{n} & =\\frac{12}{\\pi }(uv\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{n}[x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{n}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{n}(\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))+\\frac{1}{n}{[\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)]}_{0}^{\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\pi }(-\\frac{\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )}{n}+\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))) \\\\  & =-\\frac{12\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )}{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )=(-1)^{n},$ we have\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=-\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{n}=\\frac{12(-1)^{n+1}}{n}.\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363878 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363879 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [175921863