,12).$ What is the value of $f(-4)?$\n\n$f(-4)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363883 1072 #uuid "0188791e-a7fa-5d1c-b905-419c47766caf" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363883 1074 "If $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [0,12),$ the odd extension of $F$ is the function $f$ such that\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}F(x), & x\\in [0,12), \\\\ -F(-x), & x\\in (-12,0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, for $x\\in (-12,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =-F(-x) \\\\  & =-((-x)^{2}-6(-x)) \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}+6x) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}-6x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-4) & =-(-4)^{2}-6(-4)=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363884 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363885 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363884 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363884 1077 "field-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363884 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363885 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363884 1080 #uuid "62443fee-fe96-5815-bb89-8967be450b9e" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363885 1081 "8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363885 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363885 1084 #uuid "669c79c2-1922-5d4f-8294-a85dd5e7d7f3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363886 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363887 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363886 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363888 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363886 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363889 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363886 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363890 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363886 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363891 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363886 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363886 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363886 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363888 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363886 1080 #uuid "0d17c4ab-d6be-5b30-b706-494795e0cd33" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363887 1081 "I only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363887 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363887 1084 #uuid "140932fa-f586-563d-9607-96c917cbdb40" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363888 1081 "III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363888 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363888 1084 #uuid "2c28fd72-ece1-5c65-9fc9-d396faabcac4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363889 1081 "None" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363889 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363889 1084 #uuid "6a65f6c1-17f8-5e2d-a643-c8eb1959ae64" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363890 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363890 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363890 1084 #uuid "d801c7c1-24b0-593b-bc5b-d8e84efc07fb" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363891 1081 "II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363891 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363891 1084 #uuid "82b95097-cf5b-58e9-bb1d-b10c2e812f5f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363892 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363893 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363892 1069 "q-342282" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363892 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363892 1071 "$$\nx(x+3){y}^{″}+(x-2){y}^{′}+4y=0\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is a **singular** point of the differential equation above?\n\n- $x=-3$\n- $x=0$\n- $x=2$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363892 1072 #uuid "ff653b13-8b67-5277-ad4c-9f98277f418a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363892 1074 "The point $x=a$ is an ordinary point of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=f(x)\n$$\n\nif both coefficients $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=a.$ Otherwise, $x=a$ is a singular point of the differential equation.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the differential equation in standard form by dividing by $x(x+3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(x+3){y}^{″}+(x-2){y}^{′}+4y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{″}+\\frac{x-2}{x(x+3)}{y}^{′}+\\frac{4}{x(x+3)}y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{x-2}{x(x+3)}\\,\\text{and}\\,Q(x)=\\frac{4}{x(x+3)}.\n$$\n\nLet's now check the analyticity of these functions at the given points.\n\n- *Neither* function is analytic about $x=-3,$ since both denominators at $x=-3$ equal zero. So, $x=-3$ is a singular point of the differential equation.\n\n- *Neither* function is analytic about $x=0,$ since both denominators at $x=0$ equal zero. So, $x=0$ is a singular point of the differential equation.\n\n- *Both* functions are analytic about $x=2.$ So, $x=2$ is an ordinary point of the differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363893 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363894 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363893 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363895 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363893 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363896 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363893 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363897 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363893 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363898 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363893 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363893 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363893 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363897 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363893 1080 #uuid "08acca3e-bb84-5168-9c50-67de5dec3326" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363894 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363894 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363894 1084 #uuid "0ab933be-d8a6-5168-9229-b4aab6bedb49" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363895 1081 "I only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363895 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363895 1084 #uuid "d89e1c21-d1dd-5f33-9785-95e68c85465d" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363896 1081 "III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363896 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363896 1084 #uuid "2d24ec4f-680a-5f70-9d7a-4e483d0a76f9" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363897 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363897 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363897 1084 #uuid "557af1e3-b08c-5247-96f6-e932bfb7528f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363898 1081 "II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363898 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363898 1084 #uuid "730e8ed3-e6f3-5a4f-8416-43d28c8e6b3d" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363899 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363900 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363899 1069 "q-342366" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363899 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363899 1071 "$$\n(x+3){y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{2}}{y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The functions $P(x)=\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{3}}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{1}{x+3}$ are analytic about $x=-3.$\n- The functions $(x+3)P(x)$ and $(x+3)^{2}Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=-3.$\n- The point $x=-3$ is an **irregular** singular point of the differential equation." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363899 1072 #uuid "39331851-2b44-5819-96f4-7d54c8cd9bd8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363899 1074 "A singular point $a$ of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=f(x)\n$$\n\nis regular if both $(x-a)P(x)$ and $(x-a)^{2}Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=a.$ Otherwise, the singular point is irregular.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the differential equation in standard form by dividing by $(x+3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3){y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{2}}{y}^{′}+y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{3}}{y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{x+3}y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{3}}\\,\\text{and}\\,Q(x)=\\frac{1}{x+3}.\n$$\n\nLet's now check each statement in turn.\n\n- Since the denominators of both $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ vanish at $x=-3,$ they are *not* analytic about $x=-3.$ So, statement I is false.\n\n- The function\n\n$$\n(x+3)P(x)=(x+3)\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{3}}=\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{2}}\n$$\n\n is *not* analytic about $x=-3$ since its denominator vanishes at $x=-3.$ Therefore, statement II is false.\n\n- Since statement I is false, $x=-3$ is a singular point. Also, since statement II is false, it follows that $x=-3$ is an **irregular** singular point. Thus, statement III is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363900 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363901 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363900 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363902 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363900 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363903 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363900 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363904 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363900 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363905 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363900 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363900 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363900 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363902 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363900 1080 #uuid "200e14ff-e4d1-57ae-9ea3-19076e82d0d3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363901 1081 "I only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363901 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363901 10