(\\lambda +n)^{2}-(\\lambda +n)){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1}, \\\\ -6{y}^{′} & =-6\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }6(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Consolidate all the series into a single series that is equal to $0.$\n\nCollecting the terms for $n=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}-6\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1} & = \\\\ (3{\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda -6\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1} & = \\\\ (3{\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}. & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, collecting terms for $n\\ge 1,$ we obtain an infinite series of the form ${x}^{\\lambda -1}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n},$ for some ${b}_{n}(\\lambda ),$ $n\\ge 1.$\nTherefore, substituting into the homogeneous ODE, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3{\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}+{x}^{\\lambda -1}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n} & =0 \\\\ 3({\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda ){a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 5**:  Set the coefficients of the series equal to $0.$\n\nSetting the coefficients of the $n=0$ term equal to $0$ with arbitrary ${a}_{0}\\ne 0,$ we obtain the indicial equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3({\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda ){a}_{0} & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363958 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363959 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363958 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363960 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363958 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363961 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363958 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363962 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363958 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363963 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363958 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363958 1077 "selection" 131941395334