the function $f(x,y)=4x-3y-1$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $c=-1$ gives a line\n- $c=0$ gives the axes $x=0$ and $y=0$\n- $c=2$ gives a parabola" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364054 1072 #uuid "036af2f8-8d3f-5a9f-9714-c21bb558dc15" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364054 1074 "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-3y-1 & =c \\\\ 4x-3y-(c+1) & =0 \\\\ y & =\\frac{4}{3}x-\\frac{c+1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=-1$ then the level curve is $y=\\frac{4}{3}x,$ which is a line.\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curve is $y=\\frac{4}{3}x-\\frac{1}{3},$ which is a line different to the axes $x=0$ and $y=0.$\n\n- If $c=2$ then the level curve is $y=\\frac{4}{3}x-1,$ which is not a parabola.\n\nSo, only statement I is true." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364055 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364056 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364055 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364057 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364055 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364058 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364055 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364059 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364055 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364060 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364055 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364055 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364055 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364058 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364055 1080 #uuid "5e2961e2-c4d5-5918-ab70-c6f6a98c5129" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364056 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364056 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364056 1084 #uuid "1aa93218-27b0-5ad5-8222-b7e37e2e20e4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364057 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364057 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 1759218604