5585 true] [17592186364098 1069 "q-37631" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364098 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364098 1071 "Determine if the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]$\nis diagonalizable or not, and if it is diagonalizable, find a corresponding diagonal matrix $D.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364098 1072 #uuid "e3ab5a48-4ec0-5b84-8cff-a429fb97fc59" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364098 1074 "First, we find the eigenvalues of the matrix $A$ by solving $det(A-\\lambda I)=0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-2-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ -3 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-2-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-(3)(-3) & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +1 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\lambda }_{2}=1.$ Since we get one repeated eigenvalue, the matrix might not be diagonalizable. To check this, we row-reduce the matrix $(A-1I)\\text{x}=0:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-1I & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has only $1$ pivot column. This implies that we will have only $2-1=1$ linearly independent eigenvector corresponding to the current eigenvalue. Therefore, $A$ is not diagonalizable." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364099 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364100 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364099 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364101 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364099 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364102 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364099 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364103 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364099 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364104 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [1