487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364136 1071 "![](images/db/db81a26f1761db677e083d724f3ccb0a8963b9de528c15048bf66cea4aca6179.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)$ and the $x$-axis between $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ as shown above. Find the area of the region." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364136 1072 #uuid "d53d0a4e-a01f-57ae-9126-10a873bc7b52" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364136 1074 "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x){|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =1-\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\sqrt{2}-1.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364137 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364138 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364137 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364139 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364137 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364140 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364137 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364141 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364137 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364142 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364137 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364137 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364137 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364141 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364137 1080 #uuid "08ffcee2-bec0-577c-a610-f9493369cb2d" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364138 1081 "\\sqrt{6}-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364138 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 175921860