3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364177 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364177 1071 "Find the equation of the level curve that passes through the point $T(2,1)$ for the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{x-{y}^{2}}.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364177 1072 #uuid "ae2ee110-6028-560b-b154-cea2add1f458" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364177 1074 "First, we find the value of the function at $T$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2,1) & =\\frac{1}{2-{1}^{2}}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the level curve that passes through $T(2,1)$ is the $1$-level curve.\n\nRecall that the level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=1.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\frac{1}{x-{y}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ 1 & =x-{y}^{2} \\\\ x & =1+{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level curve that passes through $T(2,1)$ is the parabola $x=1+{y}^{2}.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364178 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364179 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364178 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364180 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364178 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364181 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364178 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364182 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364178 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364183 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364178 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364178 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364178 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364179 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364178 1080 #uuid "5829d29b-d41b-548e-a76a-f71d52e87bf5" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364179 1081 "x=1+{y}^{2}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364179 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364179 1084 #uuid "b1fe7f12-1aba-53b8-84a6-c65a5b3db079" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364180 1081 "y=2+{x}^{2}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364180 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364180 1084 #uuid "757f29e0-0793-5816-a02a-c5609b14f555" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364181 1081 "y=1+{x}^{2}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364181 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364181 1084 #uuid "03d173bd-9735-589b-ae2b-0f0a570f3cc4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364182 1081 "x=1+2{y}^{2}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364182 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364182 1084 #uuid "2e380ecf-c597-530c-bacd-d038a0e62d9d" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364183 1081 "x=2-{y}^{2}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364183 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364183 1084 #uuid "3eeebbe3-4754-5082-87d4-a82c718991e4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364184 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364185 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364184 1069 "q-71201" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364184 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364184 1071 "Find the equation of the level curve that passes through the point $M(2,3)$ for the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2{y}^{2}-15.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364184 1072 #uuid "769b357f-4fb6-5958-a803-d881c01aed36" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364184 1074 "First, we find the value of the function at $M$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2,3) & =\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2}+2(3)^{2}-15=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the level curve that passes through $M(2,3)$ is the $5$-level curve.\n\nRecall that the level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=5.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2{y}^{2}-15 & =5 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2{y}^{2} & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level curve that passes through $M(2,3)$ is the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2{y}^{2}=20.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364185 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364186 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364185 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364187 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364185 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364188 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364185 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364189 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364185 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364190 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364185 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364185 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364185 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364190 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364185 1080 #uuid "bc0fc72b-f01f-5a55-9f63-17e0f1879f6f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364186 1081 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-2{y}^{2}=20" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364186 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364186 1084 #uuid "8a86f79f-60fc-5217-9c6b-a03f33f604de" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364187 1081 "2{x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=20" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364187 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364187 1084 #uuid "908be2b8-6e9b-571a-8f86-e456deb80232" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364188 1081 "{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}=20" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364188 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364188 1084 #uuid "8cd8e1a5-58ec-5407-b39e-0663ce69ce38" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364189 1081 "2{x}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=20" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364189 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364189 1084 #uuid "475201b1-53d3-5bd4-b0f0-119e6038ce74" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364190 1081 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2{y}^{2}=20" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364190 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364190 1084 #uuid "94ca828d-54b6-5990-afc7-c4497e745042" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364191 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364192 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364191 1069 "q-71398" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364191 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364191 1071 "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+2y}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $c=0$ gives a circle\n- $c=1$ gives a hyperbola\n- $c=2$ gives a parabola" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364191 1072 #uuid "d3aaf864-2fae-5bdc-a851-6e2a3303364c" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364191 1074 "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+2y} & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}+2y & ={c}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curve is $y=-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2},$ which is not a circle.\n\n- If $c=1$ then the level curve is $y=\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2},$ which is not a hyperbola.\n\n- If $c=2$ then the level curve is $y=2-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2},$ which is a parabola.\n\nSo, only statement III is true." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364192 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364193 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364192 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364194 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364192 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364195 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364192 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364196 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364192 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364197 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364192 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364192 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186