a0cdf362-49b4-5e81-91f4-944c2a137d99" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364254 1074 "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $(-1,4)\\cup (6,7)$ is open. It consists of two parts, where the boundary points are $-1$, $4$, $6$, and $7.$ None of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other sets are not open because:\n\n- $(-2,1]\\cup [3,9)$ has four boundary points $-2$, $1$, $3$, and $9$, and the points $1$ and $3$ lie in the set.\n\n- $[4,6)\\cup (9,11)$ has four boundary points $4$, $6$, $9$, and $11$, and the point $4$ lies in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364255 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364256 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364255 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364257 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364255 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364258 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364255 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364259 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364255 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364260 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364255 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364255 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364255 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364258 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364255 1080 #uuid "531480b0-2b5e-5d39-b602-bae56ec77aeb" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364256 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364256 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364256 1084 #uuid "9d6fc105-4665-5793-840a-d38f2e07c65f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364257 1081 "I only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364257 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364257 1084 #uuid "3e75ea62-d875-500e-b00a-ad8139208c21" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364258 1081 "III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364258 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364258 1084 #uuid "f27839c1-6f71-56a5-b057-e5734e69d496" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364259 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364259 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364259 1084 #uuid "f06b782e-2708-5653-9046-5d9e5df40d3b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364260 1081 "II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364260 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364260 1084 #uuid "e7817c5e-15e4-5414-b3d3-9f16dd15eb81" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364261 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364262 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364261 1069 "q-71889" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364261 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364261 1071 "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<x<0,\\,0<y<-x}.\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<x<0,\\,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364261 1072 #uuid "7861d2f7-e3b6-5b7c-a05b-2009b500c4e2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364261 1074 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/40/4073e99607c1e824f67b24bc93955b39c5b320901cd391ff3adb51444d1e1416.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/79/79e005cc03bb625657c652324db58db653882c640e94ea4b21a386676745bd14.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<x<0,\\,0<y<-x}.\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364262 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364263 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364262 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364264 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364262 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364265 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364262 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364266 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364262 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364267 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364262 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364262 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364262 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364266 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364262 1080 #uuid "62bd90ab-e399-5c06-9682-cc9127123490" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364263 1081 "-x<y<0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364263 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364263 1084 #uuid "d45f5dce-fcd5-570f-8c31-3764767c0f91" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364264 1081 "0\\le y\\le -x" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364264 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364264 1084 #uuid "0f01e28b-52d6-5e0a-8ffd-a45d4df949a6" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364265 1081 "0<y\\le -x" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364265 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364265 1084 #uuid "06cc12c1-1f6e-5156-a18b-4ebea4dadd4a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364266 1081 "0<y<-x" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364266 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364266 1084 #uuid "aa30e3db-c47d-5d33-9a49-d7ba9c6e61f5" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364267 1081 "-x\\le y<0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364267 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364267 1084 #uuid "860d3ddb-5c51-56aa-8d19-8e1116fb9fae" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364268 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364269 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364268 1069 "q-72742" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364268 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364268 1071 "Suppose $X$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $det(X)=10.$ What is the value of $det(6X)?$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364268 1072 #uuid "409f716a-c0ac-55a0-a174-94c6fcabcec4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364268 1074 "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot X)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(X).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=6$ and $n=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(6X) & ={6}^{3}\\cdot det(X) \\\\  & =216\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =2160.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364269 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364270 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364269 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364271 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364269 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364272 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364269 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364273 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364269 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364274 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364269 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364269 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364269 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364273 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364269 1080 #uuid "37d4f007-41c0-5c4c-afc3-772d63dabd28" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364270 1081 "180" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364270 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364270 1084 #uuid "7e82175b-bea8-5a74-b02e-c936593b97ce" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364271 1081 "60" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364271 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364271 1084 #uuid "74d9c464-c1d9-5c1c-9898-e524d4a223c8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364272 1081 "7\\,290" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364272 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364272 1084 #uuid "cfcadc6e-ae48-50b5-a73e-be1bd42f023b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364273 1081 "2\\,160" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364273 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364273 1084 #uuid "1686ccc1-a296-5e34-a4b0-5717f1e9a359" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364274 1081 "360" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364274 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364274 1084 #uuid "6466ade6-6672-5f9b-a85e-d500d5002105" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364275 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364276 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364275 1069 "q-72745" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364275 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364275 1071 "Suppose $C$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $det(C)=-2.$ What is the value of $det(-3C)?$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364275 1072 #uuid "9fd9cb32-6a50-5911-803f-5c6dda15fae8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364275 1074 "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot C)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=-3$ and $n=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(-3C) & =(-3)^{4}\\cdot det(C) \\\\  & =81\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-162.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364276 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364277 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364276 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364278 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364276 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364279 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364276 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364280 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364276 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364281 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364276 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364276 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364276 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364278 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364276 1080 #uuid "52eaa776-c897-5d7f-9799-04b42b8b709d" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364277 1081 "343" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364277 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364277 1084 #uuid "82735552-a9a0-5138-a9bd-eda2cbacdf78" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364278 1081 "-162" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364278 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364278 1084 #uuid "3a972f69-e89e-5fdd-bba7-840c358f4374" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364279 1081 "-18" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364279 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364279 1084 #uuid "51f56c30-be4b-59a2-92cd-51fabcc72532" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364280 1081 "-81" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364280 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364280 1084 #uuid "0d018ad6-2d06-5636-89a1-57f52a9d1163" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364281 1081 "81" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364281 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364281 1084 #uuid "83917445-bd21-5048-9335-fe5e61f7489a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364282 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364283 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364282 1069 "q-73749" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364282 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364282 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=1 \\\\ 2x+6y=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364282 1072 #uuid "a9a9e509-4293-5590-b2bf-432eea2f6134" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364282 1074 "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=1 \\\\ 0x+0y=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=1$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=1,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364283 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364284 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364283 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364285 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364283 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364286 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364283 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364287 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364283 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364288 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364283 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13