mbrella, then it's a sunny day." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364490 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364490 1084 #uuid "40c31dcb-ed0e-54af-ac8a-655d71f84dad" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364491 1081 "If you use an umbrella, then it's not a sunny day." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364491 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364491 1084 #uuid "b12e36eb-f33f-5c9b-a9ad-d7e6eaa2d8fe" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364492 1081 "If it's not a sunny day, then you use an umbrella." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364492 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364492 1084 #uuid "45c52261-2f11-50ae-84e5-7f6d50f78b82" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364493 1081 "If it's a sunny day, then you do not use an umbrella." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364493 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364493 1084 #uuid "a019a6b4-8d31-591a-bb27-fa69a937f648" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364494 1081 "If it's a sunny day, then you use an umbrella." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364494 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364494 1084 #uuid "5b50a51d-91d4-5c32-b5f7-79c6ed6d8442" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364495 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364496 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364495 1069 "q-82628" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364495 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364495 1071 "Find the converse of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** it is not raining, **then** you can go to the beach." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364495 1072 #uuid "be65c675-6c5f-5624-aac0-870f6ea52d51" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364495 1074 "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ It is not raining.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ You can go to the beach.\n\nThe converse of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\nB⇒A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the converse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If you can go to the beach, then it is not raining." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364496 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364497 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364496 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364498 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364496 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364496 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364496 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364501 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364496 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364496 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364496 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364498 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364496 1080 #uuid "90e4852c-a763-56e0-9da3-973fdd389ac4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364497 1081 "If it is raining, then you can go to the beach." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364497 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364497 1084 #uuid "be420b86-754d-5224-8e19-e1fb6955d136" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364498 1081 "If you can go to the beach, then it is not raining." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364498 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364498 1084 #uuid "6ffc3482-2366-56a3-9296-86930559cd37" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364499 1081 "If it is not raining, then you cannot go to the beach." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364499 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364499 1084 #uuid "94a3980e-df0b-5559-bf4a-7ff70300f7b3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364500 1081 "If it is raining, then you cannot go to the beach." 1319