mma:\n\n\"The house is old or the house is old, or it is new.\"\n\nNow, we can simplify the phrase \"The house is old or the house is old\" to just \"the house is old.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"The house is old, or it is new.\"\n\nFinally, we can write the sentence more concisely:\n\n\"The house is old or new.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364517 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364518 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364517 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364519 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364517 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364520 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364517 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364521 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364517 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364522 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364517 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364517 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364517 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364522 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364517 1080 #uuid "89dfdeeb-395d-534d-9728-473ce4fe9a5e" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364518 1081 "The house is old and new" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364518 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364518 1084 #uuid "1df174f9-02d7-5f95-be37-0afdfdbebcc8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364519 1081 "The house is not new" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364519 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364519 1084 #uuid "1802445c-c55f-5d78-ac23-0c908e677df7" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364520 1081 "The house is old" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364520 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364520 1084 #uuid "393fb955-08a5-56ad-afbe-cba85b334267" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364521 1081 "The house is new" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364521 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364521 1084 #uuid "9b408e85-9a71-58ae-b541-8367d75a0a4a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364522 1081 "The house is old or new." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364522 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364522 1084 #uuid "360980e6-d60f-503e-8f49-f1d8a63435ed" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364523 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364524 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364523 1069 "q-84266" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364523 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364523 1071 "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t>0$ is given by $v(t)=2t+{t}^{2}.$ At time $t=1$ the particle is located at the position $x=4.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=3?$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364523 1072 #uuid "956bf838-2db8-56c1-be46-024f7a67c17a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364523 1074 "The position of the particle at $t=3$ is equal to its position at $t=1$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [1,3].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(3)=x(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{3}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(3) & =4+{\\int }_{1}^{3}(2t+{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4+{[{t}^{2}+\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =4+([{3}^{2}+\\frac{{3}^{3}}{3}]-[{1}^{2}+\\frac{{1}^{3}}{3}]) \\\\  & =4+([9+9]-[1+\\frac{1}{3}]) \\\\  & =4+(18-\\frac{4}{3}) \\\\  & =4+\\frac{50}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{62}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=3$ is $x=\\frac{62}{3}.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364524 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364525 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364524 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364526 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364524 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364527 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364524 1075 #edb/ref 17