 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364557 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364552 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364552 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364552 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364554 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364552 1080 #uuid "1e3045d8-adea-5bb9-9d6c-82806c0014f1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364553 1081 "(M∨P)∧Q" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364553 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364553 1084 #uuid "2ea9cfcc-cbdf-5f1d-a91b-944ff490bedc" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364554 1081 "Q∨(M∧P)" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364554 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364554 1084 #uuid "2c0d041b-03e8-5a66-9879-fb8fbdafc3c4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364555 1081 "M∧(Q∨P)" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364555 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364555 1084 #uuid "7e86a867-4cb2-5de4-8c5e-72244f752726" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364556 1081 "P∨(M∧Q)" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364556 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364556 1084 #uuid "9b49adfb-0c7a-57c0-b455-9c318745826d" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364557 1081 "Q∧(M∨P)" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364557 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364557 1084 #uuid "79f539e4-35e0-5de8-b8cc-e91c09ff2f6c" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364558 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364559 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364558 1069 "q-89278" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364558 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364558 1071 "Identify the sentence that is equivalent to the following: \"The car is red, and it is sporty.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364558 1072 #uuid "3dd6015e-c1e5-5397-9103-e533122d32dc" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364558 1074 "First, let's write the sentence more concisely:\n\n\"The car is red and sporty.\"\n\nUsing the commutative law, we can swap the order of the words \"red\" and \"sporty.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"The car is sporty and red.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364559 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364560 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364559 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364561 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364559 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364562 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364559 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364563 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364559 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364564 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364559 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364559 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364559 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364561 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364559 1080 #uuid "6b643251-72d1-5ece-8c4d-ad2186485bc1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364560 1081 "The car is sporty but not red" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364560 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364560 1084 #uuid "bb8f0610-7280-577b-ad4e-ca1a41548341" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364561 1081 "The car is sporty and red" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364561 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364561 1084 #uuid "3dc88fe2-b5b9-5d35-b3a2-6e7e85c56194" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364562 1081 "The car is  red" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364562 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364562 1084 #uuid "4a79abff-7f20-5d5a-8360-59dbceb3b215" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364563 1081 "The car is not sporty nor red" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364563 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364563 1084 #uuid "544907e4-8ace-5ce6-8495-bc4b3f193320" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364564 1081 "The car is sporty" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364564 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364564 1084 #uuid "886c4490-7afe-5d52-9602-d61f5e863584" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364565 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364566 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364565 1069 "q-90912" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364565 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364565 1071 "Given that ${y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is a solution to the equation ${y}^{″}+y=0,$ use reduction of order to find a second solution ${y}_{2}(x)$ to the equation, and write down the general solution." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364565 1072 #uuid "e072db4c-ae23-5874-8e05-5e0e80f81647" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364565 1074 "According to the reduction of order method, we let ${y}_{2}=u(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ \n\nDifferentiating the above with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′} & ={u}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-u\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″} & ={u}^{″}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2{u}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-u\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({u}^{″}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2{u}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-u\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+u\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ {u}^{″}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2{u}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =0 \\\\ {u}^{″} & =2{u}^{′}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $w={u}^{′}.$ Then our equation becomes\n\n$$\n{w}^{′}=2w\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\n$$\n\nThis is a separable equation that has the solution\n\n$$\nw={c}_{1}{sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nBut since $w={u}^{′},$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}={c}_{1}{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,⟹\\,u={c}_{1}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our expression for ${y}_{2}(x)=u\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ becomes\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x({c}_{1}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+{c}_{2}).\n$$\n\nSetting ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${c}_{2}=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nFinally, because $W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})=1\\ne 0,$ we know that ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are independent (you should verify this calculation yourself).\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364566 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364567 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364566 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364568 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364566 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364569 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364566 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364570 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364566 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364571 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364566 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364566 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364566 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364567 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364566 1080 #uuid "fe6acf30-551e-5b2f-95cc-84791c4dfae6" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364567 1081 "y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364567 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364567 1084 #uuid "67952861-f148-5199-901d-802ad7eb404f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364568 1081 "y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Bx\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364568 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364568 1084 #uuid "ac8be863-428e-5b87-b241-96a67407c8ee" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364569 1081 "y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+B\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364569 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364569 1084 #uuid "107ff186-6c17-5ea7-adea-7b445653f698" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364570 1081 "y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+B\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364570 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364570 1084 #uuid "7b6b5b7d-1fb2-5652-86d6-70a0293db99a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364571 1081 "y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+B" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364571 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364571 1084 #uuid "a9b43670-c885-5264-801c-5f50ae728f32" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364572 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364573 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364572 1069 "q-94621" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364572 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364572 1071 "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R,$ and its subset $H$ containing all $2\\times 2$ matrices such that the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is equal to $0.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $H$ is closed under matrix addition\n- $H$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $H$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- $H$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364572 1072 #uuid "3e8696fa-a30e-5b2e-a6f9-20152471933a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364572 1074 "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If ${A}_{1}$ and ${A}_{2}$ are two matrices from $H$ such that the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is equal to $0,$ then \n\n$$\n{A}_{1}+{A}_{2}\n$$\n\n is a matrix where the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is equal to \n\n$$\n0+0=0.\n$$\n\n This matrix belongs to $H.$ So, $H$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $A$ is an element of $H$ such that the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is equal to $0,$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\nkA\n$$\n\n is a matrix such that the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is equal to \n\n$$\n0\\cdot k=0.\n$$\n\n This matrix belongs to $H.$ So, $H$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $H$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364573 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364574 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364573 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364575 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364573 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364576 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364573 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364577 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364573 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364578 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364573 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364573 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364573 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364576 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364573 1080 #uuid "5064ba53-0659-5afe-a7f4-717377b374e1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364574 1081 "I and IV only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364574 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364574 1084 #uuid "c14137a6-cad1-5298-b5a2-c139b65ffae7" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364575 1081 "II and IV only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364575 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364575 1084 #uuid "705418e3-f85f-51c4-ad5