 and ${a}_{2}<0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n is a matrix from $D,$ since ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2}<0.$ So, $D$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example,  if $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $k=-1,$ then $A$ is an element of $D$ and $k\\in R,$ but \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =(-1)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis *not* in  $D.$ So, $D$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $D$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364580 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364581 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364580 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364582 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364580 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364583 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364580 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364584 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364580 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364585 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364580 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364580 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364580 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364581 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364580 1080 #uuid "4832a433-2062-5a14-93ce-7c582a8f7b92" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364581 1081 "I and IV only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364581 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364581 1084 #uuid "79d4ec7e-d11b-5ec7-8c41-58fc348cc2ad" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364582 1081 