{1} & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{‖{a}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {q}_{2} & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{‖{a}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, pre-multiplying both sides of $A=QR$ by ${Q}^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & ={Q}^{T}\\,A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following QR factorization of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]}}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${q}_{32}\\cdot {r}_{11}=-\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 6=-4.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364607 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364608 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364607 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364609 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364607 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364610 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364607 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364611 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364607 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364612 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364607 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364607 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364607 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364609 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364607 1080 #uuid "379ef46e-ea0e-5853-8ba7-b593f74e67fa" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364608 1081 "2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364608 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364608 1084 #uuid 