 $M=B+2I$ is singular, by the invertible matrix theorem, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\text{Col}(B+2I)\\ne {R}^{3},\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(B+2I)\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364627 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364628 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364627 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364629 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364627 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364630 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364627 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364631 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364627 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364632 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364627 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364627 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364627 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364628 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364627 1080 #uuid "db73dc06-a582-5ddd-9457-adb5f0ec282d" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364628 1081 "I, II, and III" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364628 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364628 1084 #uuid "17a2de38-a526-51be-85dc-9d3ad9bcdf84" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364629 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364629 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364629 1084 #uuid "4db29910-7cd7-5d2e-ab75-c202ca721e3f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364630 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364630 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364630 1084 #uuid "036076bf-321f-5de0-8688-b4ed7b720620" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364631 1081 "I only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364631 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364631 1084 #uuid "3180fd57-4d23-5261-afe9-a98997a0c7a8" 13194139533445 1759218